 \section{Discussion, limitations, and falsifiable use}
 The ledger is conditional on classifying charged operations correctly. Bennett's reversibility boundary prohibits interpreting it as a universal energy tax on every logic step. Real systems may add leakage, refresh, communication, cooling, finite-reservoir corrections, and nonuniform floors. The three-window model also omits time-coupled storage and thermal state.
